  "imageName": "person.slash",
  "intro": "Advanced impersonal constructions express states, necessities, and judgments without naming a subject. TYPES: 1) Dative experiencer: Мне холодно (I'm cold). 2) Modal: Нужно работать (One must work). 3) Evaluative: Трудно понять (It's hard to understand). 4) Weather/nature: Темнеет (It's getting dark). 5) General statements: Говорят, что... (They say that...). These constructions are very common in Russian and often have no direct English equivalent. The logical subject (experiencer) is in dative case.",
  "rules": [
    "Dative experiencer: Мне (dat) + state: Мне холодно, скучно, весело",
    "Modal impersonals: надо/нужно/можно/нельзя + infinitive + dative",
    "Evaluative: трудно/легко/интересно + infinitive",
    "Weather verbs: светает, темнеет, вечереет (no subject possible)"
  ],
  "examples": [
    "Мне не спится. (I can't sleep., lit. 'To me it doesn't sleep.')",
    "Здесь пахнет цветами. (It smells of flowers here.)",
    "Его знобит. (He has chills.)",
    "Нам пора идти. (It's time for us to go.)"
  ],
